# Shared UI conventions

## What belongs here

| Layer | Location | Examples |
|-------|----------|----------|
| Atoms | `components/<name>/` | Button, Input, Tag, Dropdown |
| Molecules | `components/<name>/` | TableFilters, ModalWrapper, FlowWizard |
| Hooks | `hooks/` | useFormHook, useModal, useToggle, useUpload |
| API client | `api/` | useFetch, usePost, apiGet, errorSerializer |
| Utils | `utils/` | format, stock helpers |

Domain-specific UI (product forms, category tree admin) stays in the app module unless both apps need it.

## Component checklist

1. Export from `components/<name>/index.ts` and re-export in `components/index.ts`
2. Use Tailwind classes consistent with existing components (gray palette, rounded-xl, border-gray-200)
3. Accept `className` where layout flexibility is needed
4. No app-specific imports (`admin-web`, `store-web`, `admin-api`)

## Extending forms

To add a new field type:

1. Create `components/inputs/components/MyField.tsx` using `useFieldContext`
2. Export from `components/inputs/components/index.ts`
3. Register in `hooks/useFormHook.tsx` `fieldComponents`
